Closing odds, used only to score the model against the market
    tennis-data.co.uk. Workbooks are downloaded by the user and not
    redistributed. tools/odds/ holds only the loader.


Numbers that ARE in this repository
-----------------------------------

Four small files hold fitted model parameters:

    fitted_params.json      scalar hyper-parameters (half-life, form scale,
                            calibration slope, and similar)
    fitted_curves.json      residual curves as bucket means plus row counts
    tour_avg.json           tour-average serve rate by surface and era
    confidence_model.json   measured log loss per confidence band

These are aggregate measurements — scalars and bucket means. They contain no
player, no match, and no row of the source data, and they cannot be used to
reconstruct any of it. They are published on the view that an aggregate
statistic is not an adaptation of the database it was measured from.

If you take a stricter view of ShareAlike than that, delete those four files;
`python3 tennis.py fit` and `python3 tools/curves.py write` regenerate them
from data you fetched yourself.

    matchgrid.npz
    gamesgrid.json

are tabulated output of the Barnett-Clarke recursion — the mathematics of
tennis scoring, computed from the rules of the game. No match data is involved
at any point. They are included because rebuilding them costs several minutes
of CPU for a result that is identical for everyone.
